Z||000003||Rob S||09-15-2000||05:37 PM||||I'm sure Mr. Mike's is good stuff, one question I had for them is that on their page they say the new carpet goes over top of the old stuff. ("Installs easily over the original carpet for a fast, flawless, professional job").  Does their carpet come with a padded back or do you need the old carpet? I tried to call and ask about that but it was after store hours, so I'll try again later. Thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-15-2000||08:47 PM||||The way he explained it to me (I may have this slightly wrong) was something like this:  You have to pull the backing off of the new carpet, then lay it down over the old carpet.  The old carpet is supposed to make a better padding than the jute backing alone.  Something like that.||||reg||1
